{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01032",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.57,
      "end_seconds": 7.51,
      "duration_seconds": 6.94,
      "text": "Yeah, hello doctor, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.53,
      "end_seconds": 13.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.7,
      "end_seconds": 25.05,
      "duration_seconds": 10.35,
      "text": "Mm, I'm here because of cramping pain in the lower tummy. I've been reading about it online and it worried me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.94,
      "end_seconds": 28.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.46,
      "end_seconds": 32.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "it's been about three months now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.62,
      "end_seconds": 35.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Anything that improves it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.04,
      "end_seconds": 40.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "It settles a little with passing stool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.5,
      "end_seconds": 43.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.97,
      "end_seconds": 69.33,
      "duration_seconds": 23.36,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get alternating constipation and loose stools as well. I've had bloating too, for two years. The alternating constipation and loose stools? That's been for about three months. About alternating constipation and loose stools, it's severe, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.68,
      "end_seconds": 75.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "And what about blood in the stool, fever or night-time diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.53,
      "end_seconds": 80.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "No, um, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.37,
      "end_seconds": 84.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.62,
      "end_seconds": 88.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.09,
      "end_seconds": 91.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.89,
      "end_seconds": 94.85,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "No, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.29,
      "end_seconds": 103.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.68,
      "end_seconds": 114.89,
      "duration_seconds": 10.21,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette. My partner and our baby. I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.12,
      "end_seconds": 133.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.76,
      "end_seconds": 138.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "No, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.09,
      "end_seconds": 142.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.47,
      "end_seconds": 150.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "It's escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety. Colospa, when it cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 151.99,
      "end_seconds": 155.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.16,
      "end_seconds": 159.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Anxiety, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.02,
      "end_seconds": 168.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.11,
      "text": "Yes, anxiety is known to us, good to have that clear. Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.33,
      "end_seconds": 177.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Just my tonsils removed, as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.01,
      "end_seconds": 198.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.35,
      "end_seconds": 213.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.86,
      "end_seconds": 241.7,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 97 percent, temperature 37.0. And blood pressure 111 over 80, heart rate 66, respiratory rate 18."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 242.6,
      "end_seconds": 244.42,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "is that that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.25,
      "end_seconds": 262.65,
      "duration_seconds": 16.4,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers. Right, here's what I'm thinking. This is probably irritable bowel syndrome as a working diagnosis. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. We shouldn't forget coeliac disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.9,
      "end_seconds": 288.46,
      "duration_seconds": 18.56,
      "text": "I'll request a coeliac test, it'll help with bloating. We should do blood tests for bowel symptoms. Note down what you ate before the bad days, it often reveals a pattern. I'd like to see you again after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.89,
      "end_seconds": 292.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "alright, I'll be back"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.75,
      "end_seconds": 296.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 297.8,
      "end_seconds": 301.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "I, I think I understand everything. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}